+# GPIO MMIO Latch Driver Implementation Summary
+
+## Overview
+This driver implements a generic GPIO controller for an external latch-backed, memory-mapped output port (e.g., 74HC574 latched onto an FMC bank) for Zephyr RTOS.
+
+## Files Created/Modified
+
+### 1. Driver Source
+- **File**: `/testbed/drivers/gpio/gpio_mmio_latch.c`
+- **Description**: Main driver implementation
+- **Key Features**:
+  - Output-only operation
+  - Software shadow of output value (for write-only latches)
+  - Support for 8/16/32-bit register widths
+  - Configurable number of GPIO lines (ngpios)
+  - Masked write operations
+  - Set/clear/toggle bit operations
+  - Pin configuration with initial high/low levels
+  - Initial output value from device tree
+  - Rejection of unsupported configurations
+
+### 2. Kconfig Configuration
+- **File**: `/testbed/drivers/gpio/Kconfig.mmio_latch`
+- **Kconfig Option**: CONFIG_GPIO_MMIO_LATCH
+- **Description**: Driver configuration option
+
+### 3. Kconfig Integration
+- **File**: `/testbed/drivers/gpio/Kconfig`
+- **Change**: Added source line for Kconfig.mmio_latch
+- **Line**: `source "drivers/gpio/Kconfig.mmio_latch"`
+
+### 4. CMakeLists Integration
+- **File**: `/testbed/drivers/gpio/CMakeLists.txt`
+- **Change**: Added driver source compilation
+- **Line**: `zephyr_library_sources_ifdef(CONFIG_GPIO_MMIO_LATCH gpio_mmio_latch.c)`
+
+### 5. Device Tree Binding
+- **File**: `/testbed/dts/bindings/gpio/gpio-mmio-latch.yaml`
+- **Compatible String**: "gpio-mmio-latch"
+- **Properties**:
+  - `reg`: Memory-mapped register address
+  - `ngpios`: Number of valid GPIO lines
+  - `reg_width`: Register width (8, 16, or 32 bits)
+  - `initial_output`: Initial value written to latch
+  - `#gpio-cells`: 1 (pin number)
+
+### 6. Test Suite
+- **Directory**: `/testbed/tests/drivers/gpio/gpio_mmio_latch/`
+- **Test Cases**:
+  - Initialization with initial output value
+  - Valid pin configurations (output, output with init)
+  - Invalid pin handling
+  - Unsupported configuration rejection (input, pull-up/down, open-drain, etc.)
+  - Port get/read operations (software shadow)
+  - Port set masked operations
+  - Port set/clear/toggle bit operations
+  - Interrupt configuration rejection
+
+## Driver API Implementation
+
+### Supported Operations
+1. **pin_configure**: Configure pin as output with optional initial level
+2. **port_get_raw**: Read current output value (from software shadow)
+3. **port_set_masked_raw**: Write masked value to port
+4. **port_set_bits_raw**: Set specified bits
+5. **port_clear_bits_raw**: Clear specified bits
+6. **port_toggle_bits**: Toggle specified bits
+7. **pin_interrupt_configure**: Always returns -ENOTSUP (interrupts not supported)
+
+### Error Handling
+- **-EINVAL**: Invalid pin number (outside ngpios range)
+- **-ENOTSUP**: Unsupported configuration (input, pull-up/down, open-drain, open-source, interrupts)
+
+### Software Shadow Register
+- The driver maintains a `shadow` member in the context structure
+- Shadow is updated on all write operations
+- Shadow is returned on read operations
+- Shadow is initialized from device tree `initial_output` property
+
+## Usage Example
+
+```c
+/* Device Tree:
+/ {
+    my_latch: gpio-mmio-latch@40000000 {
+        compatible = "gpio-mmio-latch";
+        reg = <0x40000000 0x4>;
+        reg_width = <32>;
+        ngpios = <8>;
+        initial_output = <0xAA>;
+        #gpio-cells = <1>;
+        gpio-controller;
+    };
+};
+*/
+
+/* Application Code */
+const struct device *dev = DEVICE_DT_GET(DT_NODELABEL(my_latch));
+
+/* Configure pin 0 as output, initial high */
+gpio_pin_configure(dev, 0, GPIO_OUTPUT_HIGH);
+
+/* Set pin 1 high */
+gpio_pin_set(dev, 1, 1);
+
+/* Read current value */
+uint32_t value;
+gpio_port_get_raw(dev, &value);
+
+/* Set multiple pins using masked write */
+gpio_port_set_masked_raw(dev, 0x0F, 0x05);
+```
+
+## Compliance with Requirements
+
+✅ Output-only controller through standard GPIO API
+✅ Support for 8/16/32-bit register width
+✅ Configurable number of valid lines (ngpios)
+✅ Software shadow of last output value (for write-only latches)
+✅ Support for masked writes
+✅ Set/clear/toggle bit operations
+✅ Pin configuration with initial high/low levels
+✅ Initial output value written to latch at init
+✅ Rejection of unsupported configurations
+✅ Enabled by CONFIG_GPIO_MMIO_LATCH Kconfig option
+✅ Selected by "gpio-mmio-latch" compatible string
+✅ Device tree properties: reg, ngpios, initial_output
+✅ Returns -ENOTSUP for unsupported operations
+✅ Invalid pins return errors
+
+## Testing
+
+The test suite validates:
+- Correct initialization with initial output value
+- Proper handling of valid pin configurations
+- Correct rejection of invalid pins
+- Proper rejection of unsupported configurations
+- Software shadow register updates and reads
+- Masked write operations
+- Set/clear/toggle operations
+- Interrupt configuration rejection
+
+## Notes
+
+- The driver is designed for output-only operation and intentionally rejects all input-related configurations
+- The software shadow ensures readback functionality even when the hardware latch is write-only
+- Thread safety is ensured through IRQ locking for register updates
+- The driver follows Zephyr coding standards and GPIO driver API conventions
